Description: Fix PulseAudio assert errors in official builds
 Chromium's base/logging.h undefines assert and replaces it with DLOG_ASSERT
 in official builds. However, PulseAudio's xmalloc.h header uses assert() in
 inline functions. When Chromium code includes PulseAudio headers after the
 logging headers, the assert macro is undefined and compilation fails.
 .
 This patch adds an explicit assert define (as a no-op) before including the
 PulseAudio header in all affected files. The fix is applied to:
 - media/audio/pulse/audio_manager_pulse.h
 - media/audio/pulse/pulse_util.h
 - media/audio/pulse/pulse_loopback.h
 - media/audio/pulse/pulse_input.h
 - media/audio/pulse/pulse_loopback_manager.h
 - media/audio/pulse/pulse_output.cc
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-08

diff --git a/media/audio/pulse/audio_manager_pulse.h b/media/audio/pulse/audio_manager_pulse.h
index 95587c6..2155220 100644
--- a/media/audio/pulse/audio_manager_pulse.h
+++ b/media/audio/pulse/audio_manager_pulse.h
@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@
 #ifndef MEDIA_AUDIO_PULSE_AUDIO_MANAGER_PULSE_H_
 #define MEDIA_AUDIO_PULSE_AUDIO_MANAGER_PULSE_H_

+// Debian: Explicitly define assert as a no-op for official builds.
+// Chromium's logging headers undef assert, and PulseAudio's xmalloc.h uses assert().
+#ifndef assert
+#define assert(x) ((void)0)
+#endif
 #include <pulse/pulseaudio.h>

 #include <memory>
